Z||000006||Songman||06-27-2001||09:10 PM||||Had to go to 90 Grand Am for the HO. 89 was the regular Q4.<P>I would love to do a QuadIV Fiero. I know a lot of people hate them but I loved mine... I think they are fairly difficult to convert though, and therefore expensive. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||pherder||06-27-2001||10:19 PM||||The HO Quad 4 engines were available from 1989 thru 1994<P>The best heads were on the 89-92.<P>The most factory HP was from the W41 Olds engines in the 92-93 Olds Achieva SCX cars ~195 HP.<P>You <B>MUST</B> use the transaxle that comes with the engine because the bolt pattern for the bell housing is different from <B>EVERY</B> other GM vehicle.  The Quad style engines (Quad 4, Quad, and TwinCam) all use the same bell housing bolt pattern so any of the transaxles (Getrag for the HO Quad 4s and Isuzu 5 speeds for the TwinCams (up to 2000?) will bolt on.<P>HO Quad 4 engines <B>ONLY</B> came with 5 speeds (Getrags).  The LO Quad 4s (150-160 HP) came with either the T125 auto (like the Fieros) or the Getrag 5 speed.  The TwinCams came with either an auto (don't know if they came with an electric auto) and the Isuzu 5 speeds.<P>The SOHC Quad engines (120 HP) are junk and only came with autos (I believe).<P>HO Quad 4s were found in Olds, Pontiac, and Chevy cars.  1990 Berrettas GTZ had them (some GTZ were 3.1 V6), Pontiac Grand Ams, and Olds (several models since the Quad 4 was an "Olds" engine.)<P>Putting a Quad 4 in a Fiero is as much trouble as putting in any engine swap.  Wiring, plumbing (both coolant and A/C), and just mounting it up is custom work.  The exhaust manifold is in the rear so the entire exhaust system is <B>VERY</B> short!<P>Having done it twice, I will never do another one.<P>Paul<BR>88 Fiero Coupe w/HO Quad 4, 5 speed ... hopefully going to another Forum member!<BR>You know who you are but I will let you tell the group!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://images.ofoto.com/photos94/1/35/44/78/40/0/40784435103_0_ALB.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||1
