Z||000010||MoneypitGT||06-28-2001||03:06 AM||||By the way if you find one in a yard the IDI cover is usually gone so you can't tell by it saying HO, but you can tell by the vin, they HO had the "A" engine code, and the low output was "D". By the way I see you are from PA, have you been to EZ pull in New Ringold? There was a QUAD GTZ that was hit in the front and had most of it cut away, engine and tranny were there, and looked like it was running when it went there, had about 120 on it but you can pick everything up dirt cheap up there.<BR> Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
